 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the maintenance of a database on intellectual property",
    "basePrintNo": "S7979",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7979-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§3152 & 3155, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7979\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the public authorities law, in relation to the maintenance of a\ndatabase on intellectual property\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo establish a database of\nintellectual property in the New York State Foundation for Science,\nTechnology, and Innovation (NYSTAR).\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nAdds a new paragraph K-1 to\nSubdivision 3 of section 3152 of the public authorities law to\ninclude in the duties and responsibilities of the New York State\nFoundation for Science, Technology, and Innovation the operation and\nmaintenance of a public, interactive database of all intellectual\nproperty generated by state employees or developed through\nstate-funded research.\n\nAmends subparagraphs (x) and (xi) of paragraph (b) of subdivision 2\nof section 3155 of the public authorities law to include an update on\nthe status of such database in the annual report of the New York\nState Foundation for Science, Technology, and Innovation.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nCountless products and processes are developed in part\nwith funds invested by the State, but often these do not get beyond\nthe development stage. This intellectual property should be\ncatalogued and made public so that individuals and/or companies\ninterested in commercializing any of the property have a\ncomprehensive and current database where all such items and\nappropriate contacts are listed.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2007-2008: A.8676\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nMinimal.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
